+  # a manual split, and one briefly voided a clearance that was already recorded (clearance is per-sha). The
+  # repair is always a new branch, so the cheapest time to say so is before the commit.
+  # Appended OUTSIDE the beads managed block on purpose: `bd hooks install` rewrites only its own marked
+  # block, so this survives re-installs. Idempotent by its own markers.
+  # provision.sh HAS NO $HERE - the post-mortem above this function records that wiring a sibling call to a
+  # variable this script never defines expanded to "/identity-check.sh", -x was false and the guard never ran.
+  # So derive the directory from $0, which is the idiom used elsewhere in this file.
+  local guard_dir; guard_dir="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)"
